# Universal Geometry                                                                                                                           
  Interactive 3D model of the torus geometry described in:                                                                                    
  
  **D = T × φ⁴: The Geometry of Spacetime**

  📄 Paper: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18438693

  🌐 Live model: https://unifiedphysics.github.io/universe/geometryoftheuniverse.html

  ## Controls

  - Drag to rotate
  - Scroll to zoom
  - Right-click drag to pan
  - Time slider to explore expansion history
  - Press S to toggle UI
  - Sound checkbox for conformal time audio

  ## License

  MIT

  ## Sphere: Twin Vortices

  🌐 Live model: https://unifiedphysics.github.io/universe/liquid-universe/sphere_twin_vortices.html

  A magnetically confined sphere holding two counter-spinning vortices, with a
  measured magnetic null between them.

  The field is the sum of three divergence-free parts: two ring-shaped vortices
  facing each other with the same polarity, an axisymmetric toroidal twist, and a
  shell of inward-pointing elements that forms the confining cage (the ticks).
  Because the two vortices oppose each other, their fields cancel along the middle
  and leave a genuine magnetic null — the void. Its size is measured from the field
  gradient each frame, not drawn in.

  Particles are pushed by the full Lorentz force using the Boris integrator, so
  they spiral along field lines, mirror off the cage and travel straight through
  the void, where nothing holds them.

  Auto-balance searches for the weakest cage that still contains the plasma, and
  settles there. Cusp losses are refuelled at the vortex cores, so the
  configuration stays live rather than simply decaying.

  ### Controls

  - Drag to rotate, scroll to zoom, right-click drag to pan
  - Sliders for vortex strength, separation, swirl, cage strength, void threshold
  - Counter-spin toggle: turn it off and the void collapses to about a tenth of
    its width
  - Paper mode for a pen-and-ink view
  - Press S to hide panels, SPACE to pause
